  "style": {
    "id": "zoetrope",
    "name": "3D Zoetrope",
    "description": "Animation about animation: a bright toy turntable on a clean cream studio sweep carrying rings of small glossy sculptures, each ring holding N successive poses of one looping action (a red ball bouncing with squash and stretch on clear rods, a sprout in a terracotta pot growing, blooming and closing). Standing still it is a row of statues; spun up under continuous light it smears into a blur (deterministic multi-sample motion blur over a one-frame shutter); when a strobe locked to the spin snaps on, the room goes dark, a strobe lamp lights the disc and each station appears to animate in place; a slightly detuned strobe makes the whole animation creep slowly round the disc. Disc angle is a closed-form function of t (smoothstep speed steps, exact integral), so every frame is a pure function of time.",
